Start with the current incident
Prepare the selected asset. No forecast or saved comparison is required.

3
00:00:18,001 --> 00:00:29,000
Review the frozen observations
Status, inspection and open orders retain their source quality and timestamps at proposal creation.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Execute a separate, explicit request
A synthetic work order is acknowledged and read back. Dispatch does not repair or reopen the ride.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,001
The ride remains closed
The live asset still reports closed, with one open work order. Acceptance is not physical completion.

6
00:00:49,001 --> 00:00:57,001
Compare an authored design
Baseline access is unreachable. The separate dining design gives a 40.852 m route at assumed walking speed.

7
00:00:57,001 --> 00:01:05,000
Inspect the native before and after
Matched static native closeups show the added connection. These images are not the live camera.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:14,001
Close the connection in the query
Closing the authored connection removes the route. The query does not change the park or its scene.

9
00:01:14,001 --> 00:01:22,001
Test the unresolved entrance barrier
The step-free filter still finds no route from the entrance. Authored labels are not certification.

10
00:01:22,001 --> 00:01:27,783
Keep the evidence and the limits
Export the exact queries, responses and identities. This design query is independent of the forecast.
